actice in federal court  anymore  because no prosecutor would ever trust  them  to keep the terms of a plea agreement  secret and if you can't negotiate  with the government then your value as a  federal criminal defense lawyer is  really going to plummet  so why would someone do this well a lot  of people are speculating that paul  manafort is angling for a presidential  pardon and  that may be true there are two schools  of thought here  the first is that paul manafort thinks  he is the smartest guy  in the room and he can beat the federal  prosecutors it's not uncommon for  criminals to think that they are smarter  than they are and smarter than the  prosecutors who are going to put them in  jail  especially when it comes to white-collar  criminals like paul manafort who are  used to getting away with serving the  law and beating regulators  so it may be that manafort just thinks  he can get away with it he  lied his way into the situation and he  can lie his way out of this situation  we'll see the second school of thought  on this is that manafort is angling for  a presidential pardon  if he works with mueller he can get a  reduction in sentence but the theory is  that if he works with president trump  who can pardon him he can avoid jail all  together  that could be but there are some  problems with that because remember  manafort has been charged in both  virginia and dc  and there have been credible reports  that manafort is guilty of all kinds of  crimes in new york  as well and the problem for manafort is  that a lot of the same  conduct for which he has already pled  guilty  could give rise to state-level charges  specifically  in the case of virginia and new york he  could be convicted of  tax fraud and remember a presidential  pardon  can only pardon federal crimes which  would still leave manafort  on the hook for any state law crimes on  top of that the mueller team is probably  going to retry manafort on all of the  crimes for which the jury hung  in virginia and they will argue for an  enhancement of sentencing  for the crimes that manafort has already  pled guilty  in the latest status report the mueller  team has promised to lay out  all of manafort's lies and failures to  cooperate in great detail it's going to  be fascinating to read that document we  don't have those details right now  but they're going to argue for a  sentence enhancement but the bottom line  is that paul manafort is going to spend  a long time in either federal or state  prison  of course he could put that time to good  use by learning a new skill like  learning how to draw he could take  classes on how to draw comic book  characters by robert marzullo on  skillshare  in fact he could learn how to draw a  whole comic about a guy named super paul  who  resides in the mana fortress skillshare  is an online learning community that has  over 20 000 classes on  everything like design technology  business you name it  and the first 500 legal eagles to click  on the link below will get two free  months of skillshare  just by clicking the link the free  premium membership gives you unlimited  access to must-know topics  so you can improve your skills and learn  new things  just like paul manafort will when he  goes to prison  so click on the link and start learning  today and until next time  i'll see you in court

